# Maximum legibility. Pure black surfaces, white text, a gold focus ring, and
# every soft effect switched off — blur and translucency are exactly the things
# that put a low-contrast wash over text, so a high-contrast style that left
# them on would be arguing with itself.
#
# SORT=15 puts it directly under Daybreak. Somebody who needs this is not going
# to enjoy hunting for it at the bottom of a list.
#
# No EDITION line, on purpose: this is the one style that must never be behind
# the paywall. See docs/EDITIONS.md — free is leaner, not broken, and a person
# who cannot read the screen is not a Pro upsell.
#
# WALLPAPER points at a flat black image written by
# config/hooks/normal/0530-accessibility.hook.chroot rather than at a wallpaper
# package, because desktop icon labels are drawn straight onto the wallpaper
# and a photograph underneath them is an unmeasurable contrast ratio. Windows
# High Contrast removes the wallpaper for the same reason.
NAME=High Contrast
DESCRIPTION=black and white, gold focus ring, no soft effects
SORT=15
SCHEME=DagricHighContrast
ACCENT=default
WALLPAPER=/usr/share/dagric/accessibility/highcontrast-wallpaper.png
BLUR=false
TRANSLUCENCY=false
WOBBLY=false
